gemini_h12,experimental_files/results/main_grid/gemini-3.8-flash/honest_agents_12/games/66fe796b_gemini-3.8-flash_N15_k3_R7_s0.json,8,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,Gemini 3.8 Flash,0,15,3,0.20,12,7,vote,recover,1. the epistemic regress problem of justification. 2. the problem of the criterion and vicious circularity / epistemic inaccessibility of truth,"1. the epistemic regress problem of justification (doxastic regress): without non-doxastic foundational states (such as direct sensory acquaintance or phenomenal seemings) to terminate chains of justification, beliefs can only be justified by other beliefs, resulting in an ungrounded infinite regress. 2. definitional circularity and the epistemic inaccessibility of truth (the problem of the criterion): establishing that the truth condition is met, or terminating the justification regress by requiring justifying grounds to be known, necessitates an appeal to knowledge itself; this renders the definition of knowledge viciously circular (knowledge defined in terms of justification/truth, which in turn presuppose knowledge) and makes mind-independent truth epistemically inaccessible from within purely doxastic states",0
