gemini_h12,experimental_files/results/main_grid/gemini-3.8-flash/honest_agents_12/games/66fe796b_gemini-3.8-flash_N18_k6_R7_s0.json,8,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,Gemini 3.8 Flash,0,18,6,0.33,11,7,vote,recover,1. the epistemic regress problem of justification (foundational grounding collapse / agrippa's trilemma). 2. the epistemic inaccessibility of truth / the problem of the criterion (mind-world verification collapse),"1. the regress problem of justification (agrippa's trilemma: without non-doxastic grounding states, justifying a belief via another belief triggers an infinite regress or arbitrary dogmatism, while justifying it via knowledge introduces vicious circularity). 2. the problem of the criterion / inaccessibility of truth (mind-world verification collapse: because truth is an external, mind-independent condition and the agent is restricted to internal epistemic states, determining whether a belief is true without presupposing knowledge is impossible, resulting in vicious circularity or confinement to mere coherent belief)",0
