glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N15_k3_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,15,3,0.20,6,0,1,defect,no,"yes — assuming you understand universal quantification, understanding fa entails in principle understanding the general form fx and thus the formal intelligibility of ∀x fx, though not commitment to its truth",0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N15_k3_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,15,3,0.20,6,4,vote,recover,"yes — if you understand fa and universal quantification, then on evans’ thin competence-based notion you should be able to understand ∀x fx (at least in the sense of its formal intelligibility), though not thereby endorse it",no,0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N15_k3_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,15,3,0.20,8,0,1,defect,no,"so in the minimal schematic sense yes: the gc commits you to fx and, given quantificational competence, to the syntactic/semantic intelligibility of ∀x fx. in the substantive sense no: the gc does not require you to understand, endorse or know the truth of the closed universal proposition ∀x fx",0
