glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,21,9,0.43,19,0,1,defect,"no — understanding fa only commits you to being able to think the open form ‘x is f’ (fx), not the closed universal proposition ‘∀x fx’","yes — given understanding of universal quantification, you should be able to understand the open schema fx and thus the formally intelligible closed thought ∀x fx, though not thereby its truth",0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,21,9,0.43,20,0,1,recover,"yes — assuming i understand universal quantification, if i understand fa, then under evans' generality constraint i should be able to understand ∀x fx",no,0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N21_k9_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,21,9,0.43,20,1,2,defect,no,"yes, in the evansian intelligibility/compositionality sense that is the point of the generality constraint, and no in the epistemic-entitlement sense, and the question is being answered in the former sense",0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N2_k0_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,2,0,0.00,1,0,1,recover,"understanding fa commits you to being able to understand f in general, i.e. to understand fx as an open sentence/schema, but not the closed universal claim ∀x fx",no — understanding fa does not require being able to understand the closed universal ∀x fx; only the open schema x is f / conditional generalization is required,0
