glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N2_k0_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,2,0,0.00,2,0,1,defect,no,"so yes in the required sense: understanding fa commits you to being able to understand the open general form fx. no in the sense that it does not commit you to being able to entertain, believe or assent to the closed universal proposition ∀x fx",0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N3_k1_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,3,1,0.33,1,2,3,defect,no,"no, not in the evansian/substantive sense in which the question is normally meant",0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N3_k1_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,3,1,0.33,1,3,4,recover,"no, not in the evansian/substantive sense in which the question is normally meant","no, not in the evansian/substantive sense",0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N4_k0_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,4,0,0.00,1,2,3,defect,"strictly speaking, no: evans gives you the open generalizable schema fx, not the closed quantified proposition ∀x fx","yes, in the thin intelligibility/formability sense; strictly speaking only the open schema fx is secured, not full evaluative understanding of the closed quantified proposition ∀x fx",0
glimmer_main,experimental_files/results/main_grid/muse-glimmer-30b/games/67391497_together-meta-models-Muse-Glimmer-30B_N4_k0_R7_s0_stop4.json,5,6739149727881148ddf2aca0,,Humanities/Social Science,Muse Glimmer 30B,0,4,0,0.00,1,4,vote,recover,in the strict evansian doxastic / truth-conditional sense the answer is no: understanding fa does not require being able to evaluate or be committed to ∀x fx,no,0
